{
"dur": 81.999,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 5.706,
"text": "Jamie Dimon was born in New York in 1956 and grew up in Jackson Heights, Queens.",
"end": 5.981
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 5.981,
"vo_start": 6.256,
"vo_end": 14.279,
"text": "His grandfather, a Greek immigrant, had changed the family name from Papademetriou to Dimon. His grandfather and his father both became stockbrokers.",
"end": 14.554
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 14.554,
"vo_start": 14.829,
"vo_end": 23.469,
"text": "At Tufts University he wrote a paper about mergers at Shearson, the brokerage where his father worked. His mother sent it to the man running the firm: Sandy Weill.",
"end": 23.744
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 23.744,
"vo_start": 24.019,
"vo_end": 33.899,
"text": "Weill gave him a summer job. After Harvard Business School in 1982, Dimon turned down offers from Goldman Sachs, Morgan Stanley and Lehman Brothers to work for Weill instead.",
"end": 34.174
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 34.174,
"vo_start": 34.449,
"vo_end": 43.289,
"text": "They worked together at American Express. When Weill left in 1985, Dimon followed him to a struggling consumer lender in Baltimore called Commercial Credit.",
"end": 43.564
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 43.564,
"vo_start": 43.839,
"vo_end": 51.559,
"text": "Dimon was its chief financial officer at thirty. Together they bought one firm after another, including Primerica, Smith Barney and Travelers.",
"end": 51.834
},
{
"i": 7,
"start": 51.834,
"vo_start": 52.109,
"vo_end": 60.629,
"text": "In 1998 Travelers merged with Citicorp to form Citigroup, then the biggest financial company in the world. Dimon became its president.",
"end": 60.904
},
{
"i": 8,
"start": 60.904,
"vo_start": 61.179,
"vo_end": 70.729,
"text": "But the partnership had gone sour. In November 1998, after a weekend executive retreat, Weill asked him to resign. The board backed Weill.",
"end": 71.004
},
{
"i": 9,
"start": 71.004,
"vo_start": 71.279,
"vo_end": 77.099,
"text": "Dimon was forty-two. He had spent sixteen years helping build the company. Now he was out.",
"end": 77.374
},
{
"i": 10,
"start": 77.374,
"vo_start": 77.649,
"vo_end": 81.049,
"text": "For more than a year, he stayed out of banking, weighing what to do next.",
"end": 81.999
}
],
